---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Scheduled monitors: run collections on a schedule, store the results locally and alert

Usage: rustman monitor [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  run              Run monitors once, store the results and exit 0 (pass), 1 (an assertion failed), 3 (a request errored) or 4 (blocked): for cron, systemd timers, launchd and CI schedules
  daemon           Run every monitor of the workspace on its schedule until stopped
  status           Show each monitor's last result, uptime and latency trend
  list             List the monitors with their schedule and environment
  history          List the stored results of a monitor, newest first
  test-alert       Send a test notification through every channel of a monitor
  schedule-recipe  Print a scheduler configuration that runs a monitor
  help             Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
